*======================================================================
* video.a99 - the F18A's display modes: VMODE sets any of them (Text 80,
* Text 40, Graphics I, Graphics II, Multicolor; 24 or 30 rows; enhanced
* colour for tiles and sprites; an application may leave the graphics modes
* (app.json "omit": "graphics") and the enhanced colour and sprites ("enhanced")
* out of its kernel: the build defines NOGRAPHICS and NOENHANCED and the
* code for them is skipped), T80INI is the boot mode (Text 80, 30 rows,
* attribute per position), the colour schemes (LDSCHM, SETSCH), register
* access (VREG) and the DMA row mover (VSHIFT).  The kernel includes it;
* the loader does not.  docs/VIDEO-MODES.md is the guide.
*======================================================================
* MODES AND COLOUR SCHEMES.  A video MODE is a combination of the chip's
* registers: how the name table is read (as characters, as tile numbers), how
* many columns and rows, how colour is chosen, and where in VRAM each table
* sits.  VMODE takes a base mode and a set of option bits, writes every
* register the mode needs, loads the tables to the right VRAM addresses,
* clears the screen and sets the variables the text routines use (TXCOLS,
* TXROWS, NAMBAS, ATRTAB ...).  That last part is the point of the design: the
* text routines (text.a99) and every program that uses COLS and TXCOLS follow
* the mode without knowing which it is.
*
* A COLOUR SCHEME is sixteen palette entries, one per ROLE (kdefs.a99, 'Colour
* roles').  Cells say 'role 2 on role 1', never 'white on blue'; the scheme
* says what each role looks like.  Changing the scheme (SETSCH) rewrites only
* the palette, sixteen words in the F18A, and every cell on the screen changes
* colour at once without being redrawn.  The five schemes are in the data bank
* (databank.a99), a SAMS page the kernel maps into slot B only for the moment
* it reads them.

* LDSCHM is the pattern to copy whenever a routine needs a window that is not
* its own.  It first saves the pages slot B holds now (CURBE, CURBF) on the
* software stack; maps the data bank with PAGEB; does its work; and restores
* slot B with SETPB, so the caller finds its window exactly as it left it.
* Without that, a program that has a page of its own at >E000 would find it
* replaced by the font after any colour change.
* LDSCHM - load colour scheme SCHEME (0-4) into palette entries 0-15.  In
* an enhanced colour mode (tiles) entry 1 is then made the text colour
* (the scheme's entry 2), so that attribute 0 shows text on the page: with
* a one-plane pattern, pixel colour 1 is entry 1 and colour 0 entry 0.
* Maps the data bank into slot B and puts back what was there.  Uses
* R0-R4, R7, R12.
LDSCHM .enter
       MOV  @CURBE,R0
       .push R0
       MOV  @CURBF,R0
       .push R0
       LI   R0,PGDATA
       BL   @PAGEB
       MOV  @SCHEME,R1         scheme * 32 bytes
       SLA  R1,5
       AI   R1,DSCHEM
       CLR  R0
       LI   R2,16
       BL   @F18PAL
       .ifndef NOENHANCED
       MOV  @VMOPT,R0          enhanced colour for tiles?
       ANDI R0,>000C
       JEQ  LDS1
       MOV  @SCHEME,R1         entry 1 := the scheme's entry 2
       SLA  R1,5
       AI   R1,DSCHEM+4
       LI   R0,1
       LI   R2,1
       BL   @F18PAL
       .endif
LDS1   .pop R1                 slot B back, as it was
       .pop R0
       BL   @SETPB
       .leave
       RT

* SETSCH - make colour scheme R0 (0-4) the current one and load it.  The
* screen is not rewritten: every cell's attribute names roles, and the
* palette is what changed.  Uses R0-R4, R7, R12.
SETSCH .enter
       MOV  R0,@SCHEME
       BL   @LDSCHM
       .leave
       RT

* VREG - write F18A register R0 (0-63) with the byte in the high half of R1.
* The F18A must be unlocked (the loader did it; VMODE keeps it so).  Uses
* R0, R1.  Leaf in effect (it tail-calls VDPWR).
VREG   SRL  R1,8                the value, as the low byte
       SWPB R0
       ORI  R0,>8000           >80 | the register number, in the high byte
       SOC  R1,R0
       B    @VDPWR

* VMODE - set the display mode.  R0 = the base mode (VMT80 text 80, VMT40
* text 40, VMGM1 graphics I, VMGM2 graphics II, VMMC multicolor), R1 = the
* options added together (VO30 30 rows, VOPOS an attribute per position,
* VOTE1-3 tile enhanced colour, VOSE1-3 sprite enhanced colour, VOSPR sprites
* on, VOS16 16 x 16 sprites, VOSMG magnified).  Sets every register the
* modes use (tile layer 2, the bitmap layer, scrolling and palette selects
* off), the VRAM tables to a blank screen in the colours of the current
* scheme, the glyph set in the pattern table of the text-like modes, and
* the text routines' variables (TXCOLS TXROWS TXCELLS TXATTR NAMBAS).  The
* display is off while it works.  The VRAM map is in kdefs.a99.  Not every
* combination exists: enhanced colour tiles apply to Text 80, Text 40 and
* Graphics I; Graphics II and Multicolor ignore VOPOS and VOTE1-3, and
* Graphics II has no 30-row form.  Uses R0-R9, R12 and what PAGEB uses; slot B
* is left as it was.
VMODE  .enter
       MOV  R0,@VMNUM
       MOV  R1,@VMOPT
       BL   @F18UNL            (nothing if unlocked already)
       LI   R0,>81A0           VR1: display off while we work
       BL   @VDPWR
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       MOV  @VMNUM,R0          options a mode cannot use are dropped
       CI   R0,VMGM2
       JL   VM1
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1          Graphics II and Multicolor: no VOPOS, no tile ECM
       ANDI R1,>FFF1
       MOV  R1,@VMOPT
       CI   R0,VMGM2
       JNE  VM1
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1          Graphics II: no 30 rows
       ANDI R1,>FFFE
       MOV  R1,@VMOPT
       .endif
VM1    MOV  @VMNUM,R2          VR0-VR7 from MODTAB: 8 words a mode
       SLA  R2,4
       AI   R2,MODTAB
       LI   R3,8
VM2    MOV  *R2+,R0
       BL   @VDPWR
       DEC  R3
       JNE  VM2
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       MOV  @VMNUM,R0          Graphics I with enhanced colour: its colour
       CI   R0,VMGM1           table is the attribute table
       JNE  VM3
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1
       ANDI R1,>000C
       JEQ  VM3
       LI   R0,>8328           VR3 = ATRTAB / 64
       BL   @VDPWR
       .endif
VM3    LI   R2,VMCONS          the registers that do not depend on the mode
VM3A   MOV  *R2+,R0
       JEQ  VM4
       BL   @VDPWR
       JMP  VM3A
       .ifdef NOENHANCED
VM4    MOV  @VMOPT,R2          VR49: 30 rows (no enhanced colour built in)
       ANDI R2,>0001
       SLA  R2,6
       ORI  R2,>B100
       MOV  R2,R0
       BL   @VDPWR
       MOV  @VMOPT,R0          VR50: attribute per position
       ANDI R0,>0002
       ORI  R0,>B200
       BL   @VDPWR
       LI   R0,>B300           VR51: no sprites (none built in)
VM5    BL   @VDPWR
       .else
VM4    MOV  @VMOPT,R1          VR49: 30 rows, tile ECM, sprite ECM
       MOV  R1,R2
       ANDI R2,>0001
       SLA  R2,6               30 rows: bit 6
       MOV  R1,R3
       ANDI R3,>000C
       SLA  R3,2               tile ECM: bits 5-4
       SOC  R3,R2
       MOV  R1,R3
       ANDI R3,>0030
       SRL  R3,4               sprite ECM: bits 1-0
       SOC  R3,R2
       ORI  R2,>B100
       MOV  R2,R0
       BL   @VDPWR
       MOV  @VMOPT,R0          VR50: attribute per position
       ANDI R0,>0002
       ORI  R0,>B200
       BL   @VDPWR
       LI   R0,>B300           VR51: sprites on = 32, off = stopped
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1
       ANDI R1,>0040
       JEQ  VM5
       LI   R0,>B320
VM5    BL   @VDPWR
       .endif
       MOV  @VMNUM,R1          the geometry the text routines use
       SLA  R1,1
       MOV  @COLTAB(R1),@TXCOLS
       LI   R0,24
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1
       ANDI R1,>0001
       JEQ  VM6
       LI   R0,30
VM6    MOV  R0,@TXROWS
       MOV  @TXCOLS,R2
       MPY  R0,R2              R2:R3 = columns * rows
       MOV  R3,@TXCELLS
       LI   R0,NAMTAB
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       MOV  @VMNUM,R1
       CI   R1,VMGM2
       JNE  VM7
       LI   R0,NAMGM2
VM7    .endif
       MOV  R0,@NAMBAS
       CLR  R2                 TXATTR: an attribute table in use?
       MOV  @VMNUM,R0
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       CI   R0,VMT40
       JH   VM7A
       .endif
       ANDI R1,>000E           Text 80 / 40: a position attribute or ECM
       JEQ  VM7B
       SETO R2
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       JMP  VM7B
VM7A   CI   R0,VMGM1           Graphics I: ECM only
       JNE  VM7B
       ANDI R1,>000C
       JEQ  VM7B
       SETO R2
       .endif
VM7B   MOV  R2,@TXATTR
       BL   @VMTAB             the tables, the glyphs, the palette
       MOV  @VMNUM,R1          last: display on, with the sprite size bits
       SLA  R1,1
       MOV  @VR1TAB(R1),R2
       .ifndef NOENHANCED
       MOV  @VMOPT,R1
       ANDI R1,>0080           16 x 16 sprites: VR1 bit 1
       JEQ  VM8
       ORI  R2,>0002
VM8    MOV  @VMOPT,R1
       ANDI R1,>0100           magnified: bit 0
       JEQ  VM9
       ORI  R2,>0001
       .endif
VM9    MOV  R2,R0
       ORI  R0,>8100
       BL   @VDPWR
       SWPB R2
* the console's copy, used when it blanks the screen
       MOVB  R2,@VR1CPY
       .leave
       RT

* VMTAB - the VRAM tables for the mode VMODE has just set up: blank screen,
* the font, the sprite attribute table cleared, the GPU program, the palette.
* Uses R0-R9.
VMTAB  .enter
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       MOV  @VMNUM,R0
       CI   R0,VMGM2
       JEQ  VT2                Graphics II
       CI   R0,VMMC
       JEQ  VT3                Multicolor
       .endif
* text-like: Text 80, Text 40, Graphics I
       MOV  @NAMBAS,R0         the name table: spaces
       LI   R1,>2000
       MOV  @TXCELLS,R2
       BL   @VFILL
       MOV  @TXATTR,@TXATTR
       JEQ  VT1A
       LI   R1,(RTEXT*16+RBG)*256   the attributes: text on the page,
       .ifndef NOENHANCED
       MOV  @VMOPT,R0               or 0 (palette pair 0) in ECM
       ANDI R0,>000C
       JEQ  VT1
       CLR  R1
       .endif
VT1    LI   R0,ATRTAB
       MOV  @TXCELLS,R2
       BL   @VFILL
       .ifdef NOGRAPHICS
VT1A
       .else
VT1A   MOV  @VMNUM,R0          Graphics I's own colour table: text on the page
       CI   R0,VMGM1
       JNE  VT1B
       LI   R0,GM1CT
       LI   R1,(RTEXT*16+RBG)*256
       LI   R2,32
       BL   @VFILL
       .endif
VT1B   MOV  @CURBE,R0          the glyphs, from the data bank
       .push R0
       MOV  @CURBF,R0
       .push R0
       LI   R0,PGDATA
       BL   @PAGEB
       LI   R0,PATTAB
       LI   R1,DGLYPH
       LI   R2,2048
       BL   @VMBW
       .pop R1
       .pop R0
       BL   @SETPB
       .ifndef NOENHANCED
       MOV  @VMOPT,R0          planes 1 and 2 of the pattern table, blank
       ANDI R0,>000C           for the enhanced colour modes that use them
       CI   R0,>0008
       JL   VT4
       LI   R0,PATTAB+>800
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,2048
       BL   @VFILL
       MOV  @VMOPT,R0
       ANDI R0,>000C
       CI   R0,>000C
       JNE  VT4
       LI   R0,PATTAB+>1000
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,2048
       BL   @VFILL
       .endif
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       JMP  VT4
VT2    LI   R0,GM2PT           Graphics II: patterns blank ...
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,6144
       BL   @VFILL
       LI   R0,GM2CT           ... colours text on the page ...
       LI   R1,(RTEXT*16+RBG)*256
       LI   R2,6144
       BL   @VFILL
       LI   R0,NAMGM2          ... names 0-255 three times
       BL   @VWAD
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,768
VT2A   MOVB R1,@VDPWD
       AI   R1,>0100
       DEC  R2
       JNE  VT2A
       JMP  VT4
VT3    MOV  @NAMBAS,R0         Multicolor: names and the colour blocks blank
       CLR  R1
       MOV  @TXCELLS,R2
       BL   @VFILL
       LI   R0,PATTAB
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,2048
       BL   @VFILL
       .endif
VT4    LI   R0,SATAB           no sprites: the attribute table clear
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       MOV  @VMNUM,R1
       CI   R1,VMGM2
       JNE  VT5
       LI   R0,GM2SAT
VT5    .endif
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,256
       BL   @VFILL
       LI   R0,GPUAD           the GPU's program
       LI   R1,GPUPRG
       LI   R2,GPUEND-GPUPRG
       BL   @VMBW
       BL   @LDSCHM            the colour scheme
       .leave
       RT

* the base registers of each mode: VR0 to VR7, (>80|reg)<<8 | value; the
* display is off here, on at the end of VMODE (VR1TAB)
MODTAB DATA >8004,>81B0,>8200,>8328,>8403,>8528,>8606,>8721      Text 80
       DATA >8000,>81B0,>8200,>8328,>8403,>8528,>8606,>8721      Text 40
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       DATA >8000,>81A0,>8200,>8327,>8403,>8528,>8606,>8721      Graphics I
       DATA >8002,>81A0,>8206,>83FF,>8403,>8538,>8607,>8721      Graphics II
       DATA >8000,>81A8,>8200,>8300,>8403,>8528,>8606,>8721      Multicolor
       .endif
VR1TAB DATA >00F0,>00F0
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       DATA >00E0,>00E0,>00E8
       .endif
COLTAB DATA 80,40
       .ifndef NOGRAPHICS
       DATA 32,32,32
       .endif
* VR10, VR11, VR19, VR24-VR31 and VR47-VR48 to their power-up values; tile layer
* 2 and the bitmap layer off, no scroll, the plane offsets VOTE and VOSE use
* (tiles >800 apart, sprites >200 apart), VR15 on status register 0
VMCONS DATA >8A00,>8B00,>9300,>9800,>9900,>9A00,>9B00,>9C00
       DATA >9D80,>9E00,>9F00,>AF00,>B001,>8F00,0

* VSHIFT - move R2 rows of TXCOLS bytes in VRAM from R0 to R1 with the F18A's
* DMA engine, started by its GPU: R3 = 0 to copy forwards (from the first
* bytes), 2 backwards (from the last bytes; R0 and R1 then point at the
* last byte of each block), as overlapping moves need.  Waits until the
* GPU is idle again.  Uses R0-R4.
VSHIFT .enter
       LI   R4,GPUBUF          the mailbox: source, destination, width,
       MOV  R0,*R4+            height, stride, flags
       MOV  R1,*R4+
       MOV  @TXCOLS,R0         width: the mode's columns ...
       SWPB R0
       MOVB R0,*R4+
       SWPB R2                 ... height R2 rows ...
       MOVB R2,*R4+
       MOVB R0,*R4+            ... stride: the same
       SWPB R3
       MOVB R3,*R4+            direction; copy
       LI   R0,GPUMB
       LI   R1,GPUBUF
       LI   R2,8
       BL   @VMBW
       LI   R0,>B600+(GPUAD/256)   VR54, VR55: the GPU's address; writing
       BL   @VDPWR                 VR55 starts it
       LI   R0,>B700+(GPUAD-((GPUAD/256)*256))
       BL   @VDPWR
       LI   R0,>8F02           status register 2: bit 7 = the GPU running
       BL   @VDPWR
VSH1   MOVB @VDPSTA,R0
       JLT  VSH1
       LI   R0,>8F00
       BL   @VDPWR
       .leave
       RT



* T80INI - the boot mode: Text 80, 30 rows, an attribute per position
* (VMODE with VMDEF), and the F18A's DMA engine tested.  Called once by
* KSTART before the first module runs.  Uses what VMODE and DMATST use.
T80INI .enter
       LI   R0,VMT80
       LI   R1,VMDEF
       BL   @VMODE
       BL   @DMATST            does this F18A's GPU have the DMA engine?
       .leave
       RT

* DMATST - test the F18A's DMA engine once: 80 bytes of a pattern at
* VRAM >1500 are copied by VSHIFT to >1580 and read back.  NODMA = 0 if
* they arrived, else non-zero (an F18A whose firmware has no DMA: the
* application then redraws rows instead of moving them).  Uses R0-R4.
DMATST .enter
       LI   R0,>1500           the pattern: 0, 1, 2 ... 79
       BL   @VWAD
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,80
DT1    MOVB R1,@VDPWD          a pattern byte
       AI   R1,>0100           the next value
       DEC  R2
       JNE  DT1
       LI   R0,>1580           the destination: zeros
       CLR  R1
       LI   R2,80              80 bytes
       BL   @VFILL             zeroed
       LI   R0,>1500           from ...
       LI   R1,>1580           ... to
       LI   R2,1               one row of 80
       CLR  R3                 forwards
       BL   @VSHIFT            the GPU copies it
       LI   R0,>1580           did it arrive?
       BL   @VRAD              read it back
       CLR  R1                 the first value expected
       LI   R2,80              80 bytes
       CLR  @NODMA             DMA works, unless ...
DT2    CB   @VDPRD,R1          the right byte?
       JNE  DT8
       AI   R1,>0100           the next value
       DEC  R2
       JNE  DT2
       JMP  DT9
DT8    SETO @NODMA             no: DMA is not used
DT9    .leave
       RT

* GPUPRG - the GPU's program, copied to VRAM at GPUAD by T80INI: the
* mailbox's 8 bytes into the DMA registers (>8000->8007), then a write to
* >8008 starts the copy; IDLE until the next start.
GPUPRG LI   R0,GPUMB
       LI   R1,>8000
       MOV  *R0+,*R1+
       MOV  *R0+,*R1+
       MOV  *R0+,*R1+
       MOV  *R0+,*R1+
       MOVB R0,@>8008
       IDLE
GPUEND
